  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CNE private sector collaboration for inclusive economic development</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">CNE privatsektorsamarbete f&#xf6;r inklusiv ekonomisk utveckling</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establish solid and strategic links to involve key political, civil society and
economic actors, to promote an informed understanding of the importance of
free competition in the economic development and the country prosperity. And
support an effective adoption of a competition law</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Etablera solida och strategiska l&#xe4;nkar f&#xf6;r att involvera viktiga politiska, civila samh&#xe4;llet och ekonomiska akt&#xf6;rer, f&#xf6;r att fr&#xe4;mja en v&#xe4;lgrundad f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;else f&#xf6;r vikten av fri konkurrens f&#xf6;r den ekonomiska utvecklingen och landets v&#xe4;lst&#xe5;nd. Och st&#xf6;dja ett effektivt antagande av en konkurrenslag</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Overall Objective:

To promote the application and understanding of the &quot;Competition Law&quot; in Guatemala, strengthening technical capacity of decision makers, involved actors and promoting a culture of competition that encourages economic efficiency and positioning the country as a destination for foreign direct investment.

Specific objectives:

To contribute to generate consensus and capacity building based on the experience and knowledge of experts to improve the effectiveness of competition legislation.

To analyze current challenges and opportunities in the application of the Competition Law in order to propose effective ways of going forward.

Promote the involvement of various interested actors, including experts, companies, civil society and consumers, in the formulation of policies to promote competition.</narrative>
  </description>
